        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8860448?u=98cb6c1c142916b74dbc1cd8e12041ee4472d9af&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\"><strong>Ark</strong> is an <a href=\"https://www.r-project.org/\" rel=\"nofollow\">R</a> kernel for Jupyter applications.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Upstream: <a href=\"https://github.com/posit-dev/ark\">https://github.com/posit-dev/ark</a></p>\n<h2 dir=\"auto\">About this PR</h2>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Add <code class=\"notranslate\">ark</code> package using <code class=\"notranslate\">rustPlatform.buildRustPackage</code> with source fetched from upstream GitHub.\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>2 test cases were skipped because of failure.\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>I opened the first failed issue on the upstream <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3707546063\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/posit-dev/ark/issues/982\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/posit-dev/ark/issues/982/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/posit-dev/ark/issues/982\">posit-dev/ark#982</a></li>\n<li>The second one failed because it required <code class=\"notranslate\">rPackages.Matrix</code> but I can't set <code class=\"notranslate\">R_LIBS_SITE</code> in nextest like other R wrapper packages.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Add <code class=\"notranslate\">arkWrapper</code> with <code class=\"notranslate\">R_HOME</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">R_LIBS_SITE</code> prefixes to make <code class=\"notranslate\">ark</code> run with correctly with R and related packages.\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Following example from <a href=\"https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/blob/master/pkgs/development/r-modules/wrapper-radian.nix\">https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/blob/master/pkgs/development/r-modules/wrapper-radian.nix</a></li>\n<li>Running <code class=\"notranslate\">./result/bin/ark --install</code> successfully create a Jupyter kernel profile, but it uses <code class=\"notranslate\">ark</code> executable path instead of <code class=\"notranslate\">arkWrapper</code>. Need to manually change to <code class=\"notranslate\">arkWrapper</code> store before using in Jupyter applications. Not sure if this is something we should concern?</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>It's my first Nix package and PR. Would love to hear any feedback.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2 dir=\"auto\">Things done</h2>\n\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li>Built on platform:\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> x86_64-linux</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> aarch64-linux</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> x86_64-darwin</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> aarch64-darwin</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Tested, as applicable:\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> <a href=\"https://nixos.org/manual/nixos/unstable/index.html#sec-nixos-tests\" rel=\"nofollow\">NixOS tests</a> in <a href=\"https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/blob/master/nixos/tests\">nixos/tests</a>.</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> <a href=\"https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/blob/master/pkgs/README.md#package-tests\">Package tests</a> at <code class=\"notranslate\">passthru.tests</code>.</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> Tests in <a href=\"https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/blob/master/lib/tests\">lib/tests</a> or <a href=\"https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/blob/master/pkgs/test\">pkgs/test</a> for functions and \"core\" functionality.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> Ran <code class=\"notranslate\">nixpkgs-review</code> on this PR. See <a href=\"https://github.com/Mic92/nixpkgs-review#usage\">nixpkgs-review usage</a>.</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> Tested basic functionality of all binary files, usually in <code class=\"notranslate\">./result/bin/</code>.</li>\n<li>Nixpkgs Release Notes\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> Package update: when the change is major or breaking.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>NixOS Release Notes\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> Module addition: when adding a new NixOS module.</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> Module update: when the change is significant.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> Fits <a href=\"https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/blob/master/CONTRIBUTING.md\">CONTRIBUTING.md</a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/blob/master/pkgs/README.md\">pkgs/README.md</a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/blob/master/maintainers/README.md\">maintainers/README.md</a> and other READMEs.</li>\n</ul>\n<hr>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Add a 👍 <a href=\"https://github.blog/2016-03-10-add-reactions-to-pull-requests-issues-and-comments/\" rel=\"nofollow\">reaction</a> to <a href=\"https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/pulls?q=is%3Aopen+sort%3Areactions-%2B1-desc\">pull requests you find important</a>.</p>",
